The Mercedes-Benz Vito Tourer SELECT is a passenger-focused variant of the W447 Vito, positioned above the PRO trim and below the V-Class. It's designed for leisure and passenger transport, offering enhanced comfort and features. The most recent versions (post-2019 facelift) benefit from updated technology and design.

Here's an evaluation based on the available data for the W447 Vito Tourer SELECT:

-   **price_usd**: New prices for a Vito Tourer SELECT start around £33,000 + VAT (approx $41,800 USD). Used prices vary, with a 2021 119 Tourer SELECT L3 averaging around £19,260 (approx $24,400 USD). A 2024 116 CDI Select 9-Seater is listed at a P11D value of £63,624 (approx $80,700 USD). A 2025 model is priced at R1,375,279 in South Africa (approx $73,000 USD). Compared to the average new car price (~$52,000), the new price is around average to high, while used prices are lower. Score: -0.10 (leaning towards the higher new price range for a well-equipped van).
-   **total_cost_estimate_5yr_usd**: Vans can have varied ownership costs depending on usage and maintenance. Mercedes parts and labor can be more expensive. Reliability is generally good for the W447. Service intervals are long (up to 24,000 miles or two years). Default to average. Score: 0.00.
-   **insurance_usd_yr**: Commercial vehicle insurance rates vary. No specific insurance group found for the SELECT trim, but vans can be higher than passenger cars. Default to average. Score: 0.00.
-   **maint_usd_yr**: Mercedes-Benz parts and labor can be more expensive than mainstream rivals. Score: -0.20.
-   **repair_risk_score**: The W447 Vito has a solid reputation for reliability and consistently appears in the top 10 of the FN50 van reliability survey. Score: 0.70.
-   **hp**: Engine options for the SELECT trim include 116 CDI (163hp) and 119 CDI (190hp). A 2025 model is listed with 140 kW (188 hp). A 2021 121 Select in Malaysia has 208 hp. Averaging these gives around 170-190 hp. This is around the average for passenger cars today. Score: 0.00.
-   **torque**: Torque figures are around 380 Nm (116 CDI) and 440 Nm (119 CDI/140kW engine). The 121 Select has 350 Nm. Averaging these gives around 400 Nm (approx 295 lb-ft). This is good torque, especially for a diesel. Score: 0.50.
